CT,8,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F181A1773705835
OL,1,T]St000p4p0p0t  <4,4V]D           GA5/6
OL,2,T]S555555u5=%5  75 5V]DNEWS FROM
OL,3,T]S#!#!#!,%#!#  #! !V]DBBC CEEFAX
OL,4,V ||||||||||||||||||
OL,5,F
OL,6, Mr Lawson said he plans to increase the
OL,7, allowance for blind taxpayers.
OL,9,FThe blind person's allowance has not
OL,10,Fchanged since 1981 when it rose by #180
OL,11,Fto its present level of #340.
OL,13,FMr Lawson's proposal will increase the
OL,14,Fallowance for 1987-1988 by a further
OL,15,F#180 to #520.
OL,23,D]CFromF17-03-87C/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,182,190,120,250,0,100
