OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F181A1773705835
OL,1,T]St000p4p0p0t  <4,4V]D           GA6/6
OL,2,T]S555555u5=%5  75 5V]DNEWS FROM
OL,3,T]S#!#!#!,%#!#  #! !V]DBBC CEEFAX
OL,4,V ||||||||||||||||||
OL,5,F
OL,6, There are to be no changes on duties
OL,7, on tobacco, drink or leaded petrol,
OL,8, Chancellor Mr Nigel Lawson announced.
OL,10,FHe said there was also to be no change
OL,11,Fon the #100 vehicle excise duty, but
OL,12,Fduty on unleaded petrol would be
OL,13,Flowered by five pence.
OL,14,F
OL,15,FScale charges for people with company
OL,16,Fcars are to be increased by 10 per
OL,17,Fcent for 1988-1989.
OL,19,FMr Lawson said he would abolish, from
OL,20,FMarch 29, the tax on on-course betting,
OL,21,Fbut the duty on the gaming machine
OL,22,Flicence would rise.
OL,23,                      D]CFromF17-03-87
